# Rust build output
target/

# The reference engine and its builds, fetched rather than vendored.
# tools/build-variants.sh writes one source copy and build per
# optimisation level, and the ITU-R P.533 checkout is about 700 MB.
vendor/

# Fetched WSPR aggregates and generated per-path detail
data/

# A soak run's working files, which belong on the results branch rather
# than here.
dumps/
parity.md
flux.json
kp.json
swx.txt

# A run with a negative OUTGRAPH method writes to a Fortran unit the
# driver never opens, so the reference leaves this behind next to
# whichever directory the harness ran from.
fort.16
